  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes two hybrid quantum‑classical architectures (QNN and HQNN) based on variational quantum circuits for time series forecasting and evaluates them on four datasets (Mackey‑Glass, Lorenz attractor, Box‑Jenkins gas furnace, and USD/EUR exchange rates). Using 2–5 qubits and circuit depths between 4 and 10 on a PennyLane simulator, the QNN achieved RMSE 0.0136 on Mackey‑Glass and 0.00281 on USD/EUR forecasting, showing performance comparable to classical MLP, CNN, and LSTM models but without demonstrating computational advantage.",
